                        <h3>Promotion<br>History</h3>
                        <p>
                            Follow the journey<br>
                            to World Heritage listing.
                        </p>
                    </div>

                    <div class="sub-desc-img">
                        <p>
                            In October 2012, the Yangju City Hoeamsa Temple Site Museum was established, and upon the completion of archaeological excavations in 2015, the museum initiated its own in-house research.
                        </p>

                        <p>
                            Following the completion of the Comprehensive Renovation Project for Hoeamsa Temple Site in Yangju in October 2016—a major undertaking that spanned approximately 20 years—the city formulated a master plan to push for the World Heritage inscription of the Hoeamsa Temple Site in Yangju. This marked the official beginning of the inscription process, driven by close consultations with related organizations and heritage experts.
                        </p>

